    "context": "\"Sliding Billy\" Hamilton scored 198 runs (or 196 or 192, depending who you ask) in 132 games in 1894, an MLB record that still stands today. Babe Ruth got closest with 177 runs in 1921. Hamilton also hit .403 and stole 100 bases, including 7 in a single game, another MLB record. His Phillies finished third.",
